  (text_box "CHARGER (spec 4.1/4.7): ISET 1.82k -> ICHG ~110 mA; ILIM 1k -> 200 mA; IPRETERM 4.99k -> 10%; VBATREG default 4.2 V.\nOD-8: /CD -> P0.08 (B402 pin 50, moved from P0.25 - P0.25 does not exist) + 100k PU to V_PMID (ship-mode capable).\nBQ INT -> 100k PU +1V8, NC on MCU (read FAULTS reg, AD-029); /PG TP only. /MR -> J6 pinhole + R_MR 100k PU (+1V8) (rev A addition JP 2026-11-21: hard power-cycle recovery, USB detached). RESET NC (Nicla P0.18->MR net dropped, C3).\nLS/LDO unused (C4): LSCTRL->GND, VINLS->SYS, LS/LDO 1uF. TS: R_HI (VBUS->TS) + R_LO (TS->GND) + pack NTC - values TBD-JP (OD-4).\ni2c0 pull-ups 100k to +1V8 (Nicla parity; BQ ds suggests 10k - spec chose Nicla parity). USB-IF inrush note OD-14."
    (at 15 104 0) (size 132 26)
    (stroke (width 0.0) (type dash))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 312bd0ef-96aa-4d9a-be0f-ba90d4a11421)
  )
  (text_box "HARD RESET PINHOLE (rev A, JP 2026-11-21): J6 shorts BQ25120A /MR (E1) to GND for >64 ms ->\nthe PMIC restarts its rails = a TRUE power cycle, which is the only thing that clears a\nwedged MCU (SoftDevice/mbed hang); a soft reset cannot. R_MR 100k pulls /MR high.\nAssumption (JP): USB DETACHED - on VBUS the board stays powered, so this only restarts the PMIC.\nA soft reset button is deliberately NOT added.\nUART CONSOLE: TP_TX (P0.20) / TP_RX (P0.09) + TP_GND, 1.0 mm pads for a pogo probe.\nPOGO JIG: MH1/MH2 1.6 mm NPTH + FID1/FID2 fiducials flank the console pads. Hole pair is ASYMMETRIC on purpose (MH1 17 mm / MH2 13 mm from pad centroid) so a 180-deg flipped jig cannot seat. Pad pitch shown 5.08 mm for legibility; final PCB spacing + hole datum to be set in layout against the printed jig (JP prints it)."
    (at 15 60 0) (size 78 20)
    (stroke (width 0.0) (type dash))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 84413e3d-8fb0-492f-af1f-0c335c6acf19)
  )
  (text_box "USB-C: VBUS 10uF bulk at connector; D+/D- NC; shell stitched to GND.\nESD D5 TBD-JP (OD-13: PESD5V0U2UT vs TPD4E05U06)."
    (at 15 86 0) (size 40 14)
    (stroke (width 0.0) (type dash))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 832927b6-f63d-49f0-9e4d-ab40d5d3424e)
  )
  (text_box "GAUGE (spec 4.2, AD-029): addr 0x36 fixed; VDD(3)=VBAT sense +0.1uF; CELL(2) NC->GND; CTG/QSTRT->GND.\nALRT(5) OD -> 10k PU +1V8 -> P0.21 (B402 pin 26). OD-12: verify MAX17048 VIH vs 1.8 V pull-ups at review."
    (at 15 176 0) (size 44 16)
    (stroke (width 0.0) (type dash))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 8ca5fb5d-49eb-4221-8622-760212c43519)
  )
  (text_box "PERIPHERALS / v2 DNP (spec 2/4.3/4.6/4.8):\nSK6812-mini x5 strip: DIN <- P0.19 (B402 pin 38) through dual-supply level translator (VCCA +1V8 / VCCB +5V,\nTXB0102/TXS0102-class - part TBD-JP, OD-9). Strip supply +5V from MT3608 boost (EN -> P0.17 = B402 pin 49, moved\nfrom P0.24 - does not exist; OD-9b: keep P0.19 vs move to full-drive GPIO - decide after R2 bench).\nBoost BOM (hw doc 7.3): L 4.7uH/2A, Cin 10uF, Cout 22uF, Rfb 75k/10k, Cff 22pF. NOT drawn - capture at layout.\n32k: Y1 SIT1532AI (OD-10 default FIT) -> XL1 (pin 17); XL2 (18) -> GND; Y1 decap TBD-JP. LFRC-only = EVK alternative.\nUART console TP: TX P0.20 (pin 10) / RX P0.09 (pin 22, NFC1 - no NFC coil on board). TP set per OD-3:\n+1V8, +5V, VBAT, V_PMID, GND, BQ INT, SWD row, UART row, ALRT, LED-data.\nDNP v2 (footprints retained): LDC1612 U6 + 14mm coil (ADDR=GND -> 0x2A; INTB -> BUTTON net per OD-11; CLKIN tie\nGND if internal osc - v2), RV-3028-C7 @0x52 (/INT -> TP, no GPIO steal).\nNO BEEPER (JP 2026-11-22): BZ1 removed entirely - no footprint, no GPIO. The old note named P0.09,\nwhich is now UART_RX_TP (console pad), so it was also a pin conflict. F14/I08 corrected to match.\nnRF P0.24/P0.25 DO NOT EXIST on B402 (spec C1/C2 pin moves). Module USB (pins 21/34/35) unused - NC."
    (at 125 185 0) (size 105 46)
    (stroke (width 0.0) (type dash))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid cf29b6cd-0a6d-4679-a85f-96c5a1f45ebc)
  )
  (text_box "BATTERY / POWER TREE (spec 4.8/5): Renata ICP622540PMT 600 mAh 3.7 V LiPo, 3-wire NTC pack, JST-3 user-replaceable\n(connector PN TBD-JP, OD-4; pinout per ABX00050 = VBAT/NTC/GND). VSYS is the +1V8 rail (buck default 1.8 V, 300 mA).\nVBAT -> MAX17048 VDD only. V_PMID -> IS31FL3194. Charge 110 mA + system ~25 mA + LED ~23 mA bat-side = 158 mA < ILIM 200 mA.\nSession ~48 mAh -> ~12.5 sessions (hw doc 7); gauge adds ~3 uA (AD-029). Battery capacity 600 mAh per docs (OD-4 confirm)."
    (at 15 216 0) (size 110 30)
    (stroke (width 0.0) (type dash))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 1c52e2ab-5136-4b11-870f-248ed5aec50c)
  )
  (text_box "J3 = ARM Cortex Debug 2x5 1.27 mm: 1 VTref(+1V8) 2 SWDIO 3 GND 4 SWDCLK 5 GND 6 SWO 7 KEY-NC 8 TDI-NC 9 GND 10 nRESET(=RESET_N, B402 pin 12 - nothing else on pin 12 except TP).\nOD-2: Tag-Connect TC2050 footprint alternative (castellated pads). SWO = B402 pin 16 (optional)."
    (at 15 274 0) (size 92 14)
    (stroke (width 0.0) (type dash))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid bb4cd7c9-b54f-4398-99d1-9746a9357970)
  )

